.TH Q 1 "" "local-models"
.SH NAME
q \- quick local LLM companion: answers, shell commands, commit messages, file Q&A
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B q
[intent] \(dq<prompt>\(dq [\-\-big|\-\-code|\-\-web] [\-\-ctx FILE] [\-\-json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Quick local LLM companion: answers, shell commands, commit messages, file Q&A.
.PP
Input: a prompt, optional intent, optional document (\-\-ctx FILE or stdin).
.PP
Output: plain text; \-\-json one object; \-\-stream\-json NDJSON; \-\-format SCHEMA adds parsed .data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-big / \-\-code
use the big (reasoning) / code tier for this call
.TP
.B \-\-web
search the web first (DDG, no key) and answer from the results, cited
.TP
.B \-\-route / \-\-no\-route
force or skip the automatic routing of image paths, file paths and typos
.TP
.B \-\-diy
let q route itself with a planner pass: intent, web, file, tier, narrated in gray
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-continue [N]
continue your last exchange / entry N
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-model M
model or tier alias: small | big | code | sweep | <name> (default: small)
.TP
.B \-\-think
show the reasoning trace (dimmed, on stderr; off by default)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stats
hide the gray token line (text mode; machine modes always carry the counts)
.TP
.B \-\-raw
no system prompt (bare model)
.TP
.B \-\-json
machine mode: one JSON object on stdout, no ANSI
.TP
.B \-\-stream\-json
machine mode: NDJSON chunk/done/error lines
.TP
.B \-\-format FILE
constrain output to a JSON schema (with \-\-json: adds parsed .data)
.TP
.B \-\-glow
render the reply through glow (buffers output; TTY\-only, no\-op without glow)
.TP
.B \-\-ctx, \-\-file FILE | \-
context document from a file or stdin (\- = stdin)
.TP
.B \-\-ctx\-name S
the document's display name (framing hint)
.TP
.B \-\-sheet NAME|N
XLSX sheet to read (1\-based number or name; required for multi\-sheet describe\-data)
.TP
.B \-\-preflight
inspect extracted input, context size, and sheet selection without a model call
.TP
.B \-\-prose
describe\-data only: add optional model interpretation after exact profile
.TP
.B \-\-max\-ctx N
read at most N chars of the document (default 16000; the cut is printed)
.TP
.B \-\-timeout S
wall\-clock cap; structured timeout error after
.TP
.B \-\-intent X
intent as a flag (same set as the positional token)
.TP
.B \-\-all
with show \-1, \-c or history: include calls from other terminals, agents and hooks
.SH INTENTS
.TP
.B ask
Direct answer, <=2 sentences.
.TP
.B cmd
A single macOS shell command, nothing else.
.TP
.B code\-dispatch
Scoped code change under a pre\-written judge — the local coder as a worker, never an architect.
.TP
.B commit
A git commit message (pipe the diff in).
.TP
.B complete
Finish an unfinished code file — implement stubs to spec, output the whole file.
.TP
.B describe\-data
Deterministic row, schema, missing\-value, and numeric range profile.
.TP
.B diy\-plan
Internal: classify a prompt into {intent, web, file, image, tier, probe} for \-\-diy.
.TP
.B explain\-code
What the code does + flags dangerous bits.
.TP
.B qa
Answer grounded ONLY in the context document.
.TP
.B review
Code/PR review — bugs, risks, broken invariants, missing tests.
.TP
.B summarize
TL;DR of the context document, length\-adaptive.
.TP
.B title
A 2\-5 word title (tab titles, fire\-and\-forget).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B q \(dqhow do I check disk usage\(dq
Terse answer.
.TP
.B q cmd \(dqkill everything on port 3001\(dq
One macOS command, checked against its \-\-help.
.TP
.B git diff | q commit
Commit message from the diff.
.TP
.B q summarize \-\-file report.pdf
PDF, Word and the like extracted locally.
.TP
.B q \-\-big \(dqreason through this tradeoff\(dq
The heavier model, on demand.
.TP
.B q intents
List the available intents.
.TP
.B q show \-1
Your latest call, in full.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The work ran and failed, or a check failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage: unknown flag, missing value, unknown verb.
.TP
.B 10
Server down or a backend call failed.
.TP
.B 11
Model or backend not available.
.TP
.B 12
Input missing or unreadable (file, image, history entry, optional dependency).
.TP
.B 13
Wall\-clock timeout.
.TP
.B 127
A required program is not installed.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled by the caller.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B logs/*\-history.jsonl
One JSON line per call. History is per terminal by default; \-\-all or LM_ALL=1 reaches every caller.
.SH SEE ALSO
lm(1), see(1), warm(1), imagine, review
